WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.512
Here's how the kit makes
privilege checkable.

2
00:00:02.512 --> 00:00:07.544
A file called calls dot JSON lists
every HTTP call a Python client makes:

3
00:00:07.544 --> 00:00:11.090
the system, the method and
path, the tasks that make it,

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.213
the least privilege it needs,
and the vendor page that says so.

5
00:00:15.213 --> 00:00:18.782
A test runs the clients
against a fake HTTP session

6
00:00:18.782 --> 00:00:21.926
and fails on any call
the file doesn't declare.

7
00:00:21.926 --> 00:00:25.343
So a new call fails the test
until someone adds its row,

8
00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:30.237
its privilege and its source, and a
reviewer sees that row in the pull request.

9
00:00:30.237 --> 00:00:33.624
The test also asserts that
no task asks SailPoint

10
00:00:33.624 --> 00:00:37.176
or Graph for a write scope,
except workflow creation.

11
00:00:37.176 --> 00:00:39.600
Then the kit calls tool reads the file.

12
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.613
Give it a task and it
lists what that task needs.

13
00:00:42.613 --> 00:00:48.070
Give it a grant and it compares, and
exits one on anything missing or extra.
